  "result": "Subcommands now get their own section of the parent's `default_map`, so a map like `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` reaches `runserver` again. The existing tests pass. I didn't add a test for this case.\n\nThe bug was in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`. A child context inherited the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own command name. That meant `runserver` looked up `port` in the top-level dict and never found it. The fix is one line: `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\nI did not check what happens when the parent's entry for that name is not a dict.",
